# Stage 4d — isJuralOppositeOf on the Claim <-> NoRight axis.
#
# It cannot be derived like 04c: the content of the CORRELATIVE position is
# deliberately not materialised (it propagates through the chain
# isCorrelativeOf ∘ concernsLegalAction), so a join over contents would see
# nothing without a reasoner. It is derived where it conceptually belongs: if
# two primary positions are opposites, so are their correlatives.
#
#   Duty(A,x) opposite Privilege(A,¬x)  =>  Claim(B,x) opposite NoRight(B,¬x)
#
# Requires both correlatives to exist, which only happens if both norms name a
# counterparty. If one is missing, nothing is invented.
PREFIX norma: <https://w3id.org/def/norma-o#>
CONSTRUCT { ?claim norma:isJuralOppositeOf ?noright . }
WHERE {
  ?duty norma:isJuralOppositeOf ?priv .
  ?duty    a norma:Duty      ; norma:isCorrelativeOf ?claim .
  ?priv    a norma:Privilege ; norma:isCorrelativeOf ?noright .
  ?claim   a norma:Claim .
  ?noright a norma:NoRight .
}
